stor" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Add an investor</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Investors</b> and press <b class="gd-ui">Add an investor</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Fill in the Legal name and the Type: Individual, or Corporation with the Person who signs for the corporation. Then the Email, the Phone and the Address (start typing and choose it).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Optional: the Amount committed, and the Yearly return offered (the investor offer&#39;s, 30% unless you change it; the investment agreement sets the one that applies).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Invite now is ticked: press <b class="gd-ui">Add and invite</b>. The record is added and the investor gets the invitation to choose a password for the investor portal. Untick it to add the record only, and invite later from the list.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-send-a-password-link" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Send a password link</h2><p class="gd-p">For anyone who forgot their password or let their invitation expire.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Under People who can sign in, search by name or email.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">On their row, press <b class="gd-ui">Send password link</b>. They get &quot;Reset your CarmaCars password&quot;, valid for 24 hours.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">View as (...)</b> on the same row opens their portal, read only.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/portals</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/440"><img src="/guides/img/admin-27-portals-desktop-ee9b3e94.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="440"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:74.8%;top:6.6%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:68.2%;top:28.6%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:84.1%;top:28.6%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-view-as-see-what-someone-sees" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">View as: see what someone sees</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A red banner says &quot;Viewing as Name (email), read only.&quot; on every page.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Click around their portal. Nothing can be changed: every save is refused.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Exit</b> to come back. A view also ends by itself after 30 minutes.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/owner</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/620"><img src="/guides/img/admin-28-view-as-desktop-f858e38c.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="620"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:48.6%;top:4.5%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:94.4%;top:4.5%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>Can&#39;t change anything in Admin? You may still be viewing as someone. Look for the red banner and press Exit.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-the-audit-log" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The audit log</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Audit log</b> shows who changed what, and when.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Changes lists every change with the person, the action, the table and the record. Data access lists lookups of private data.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Every View as is recorded (view_as_start), with the person viewed.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Search by table, record id or value.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/audit</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/560"><img src="/guides/img/admin-29-audit-desktop-b7504100.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="560"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:22.6%;top:31.1%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:39%;top:46.4%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:89.6%;top:20.7%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-staff-and-roles" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Staff and roles</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Staff</b> opens Staff and roles.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Invite staff here too: Role, Name, Email, Main function and Also covers, then <b class="gd-ui">Invite</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Each row has <b class="gd-ui">Send password link</b>, <b class="gd-ui">View as (...)</b> and Limits (how much they may approve or refund).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">End access</b> to close their staff portal at once. <b class="gd-ui">Restore</b> undoes it.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/settings/staff</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/780"><img src="/guides/img/admin-26-staff-desktop-72287d0b.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="780"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:20.8%;top:59%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:94.4%;top:86.7%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:83.3%;top:92.6%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-admin-access" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Admin access</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">All settings</b>, then Admin access. Who may hold the Admin role.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The list holds rent@carmacars.ca, and verify-admin@carmacars.ca, the automated test account the site&#39;s nightly checks sign in with.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Below it: everyone who holds the Admin role now. Each must be on the list; the database refuses the Admin role to any other address.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Change the list only if the business&#39;s Admin address changes.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-staff-scorecards" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Staff scorecards</h2><p class="gd-p">See how each assistant is doing against the targets.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On a staff member&#39;s row in Staff and roles, press <b class="gd-ui">Scorecard</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">By week shows each measure (for example quote sent within 5 minutes) and the result for each week.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A task meets its target when it is done by its due time. Daily checks count when done by 9:00 and 18:00.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/scorecard</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/350"><img src="/guides/img/va-sales-05-scorecard-desktop-956a5a9e.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="350"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:21.1%;top:42.9%" aria-hidden="true">2</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-sales-by-staff-member" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Sales by staff member</h2><p class="gd-p">See each person&#39;s commissions, quotes, offers, rentals added, bookings confirmed and booked revenue.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On a staff member&#39;s row in Staff and roles, press <b class="gd-ui">Sales</b>. Press <b class="gd-ui">By week</b> or <b class="gd-ui">By month</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The tiles show the current week or month. By week (or By month) lists each period: quotes created, offers sent, rentals added, bookings confirmed, conversion and booked revenue.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Follow-ups due lists their open deals with the next step. Deals lists each booking they created, added or sent an offer on, with what it counts.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A deal credited to the wrong person, or marked sourced when it was not? Press <b class="gd-ui">Reassign</b> beside it, choose who, say whether they sourced the client, and write the reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Commission rate</b> gives this person their own flat rate (empty: the Program settings). <b class="gd-ui">Reverse</b> beside a commission stops it, for example for a household rental found later.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Staff enter their own home address (at their first sign-in, before they sign their agreement, or in their profile). It is needed before they add a rental or earn a commission, and spots a household rental. <b class="gd-ui">Home address</b> here changes it if it is wrong.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">The whole team: <b class="gd-ui">Today</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Overview</b>, the Sales card at the bottom. Choose another month and press <b class="gd-ui">Show</b>.</div></li></ol></div><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Figure</th><th scope="col">How it is counted</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Credited to</td><td>Whoever created the quote or added the rental; for a website request, whoever sent its first offer. An Admin can reassign it.</td></tr><tr><td>Conversion</td><td>Of the deals credited in the period, the share confirmed so far.</td></tr><tr><td>Booked revenue</td><td>The rental charge before tax, after discounts, for bookings confirmed in the period. A cancelled booking counts only what was kept; refunds come off.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-sales-staff-in-person-or-remote" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Sales staff: in person or remote</h2><p class="gd-p">Each Sales person works in person (Toronto) or remote (anywhere, a contractor). Staff and roles lists them under Sales staff: in person or remote.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Work mode</b> on a person (or on their Sales page), choose In person or Remote and give the reason. A new Sales person starts in person.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The list shows the mode, the rate now, the rate the month would end at, and for remote this month&#39;s touches against 400, the peak hours scheduled this week (20 needed, Thursday to Sunday afternoons) and the replies on time.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">On a remote person&#39;s Sales page, Remote duties shows their checklist, touches, blocks and reply time. <b class="gd-ui">Void</b> beside a touch logged by mistake takes it off, with a reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">When you approve a Sales month, its mode, rates, touches and any drop are locked: a later change of mode or settings does not change it. Their My sales shows each month in one line.</div></li></ol></div><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col"></th><th scope="col">Rule</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Rates</td><td>In person 10%, 15% from 50 rental days, 20% from 100. Remote 5 points lower on every tier: 5%, 10%, 15%</td></tr><tr><td>Credit</td><td>In person: walk-ins, handovers, partner visits and the rentals they source. Remote: only the rentals they source; a website request they answer with the first offer during their blocks is credited to them; a walk-in or a partner deal earns them nothing</td></tr><tr><td>Remote minimum</td><td>400 touches a month. Under it, when the month ends, the month&#39;s rate is one tier lower (5% becomes 2.5%). Settings &gt; Program settings, Staff commissions, changes the minimum, the drop and the floor</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'data-health', 'chapter', 'email-backups-and-site-health', null, 'Data health', 'The nightly self-check on To do: what it finds, the one-tap fixes, what it fixes by itself, and test accounts.',
  'Every night the database checks its own records for the mistakes people used to spot by hand, fixes the clear-cut ones itself and lists the rest for you on one card.

## The Data health card

**Today** > **To do**, the Data health card below the usage cards.

1. The card says when it last checked. Press **Check now** to run it again.
2. Each line is one kind of problem with its count, for example "2 Confirmed bookings whose pickup time passed with no pickup recorded". All clear shows "All 17 checks clear."
3. Press a line to open its records. Each record links to its page.
4. Where the fix is safe, the record has its button: **Mark picked up**, **Close**, **Unassign**, **Restart follow-up** or **Close** for a task. The record leaves the card at once.
5. The last line says what was fixed without asking this week.

> Good to know: One in-app notice a day tells Admins when the night''s check found something. It is never emailed or texted.

## What it checks

- Confirmed bookings whose pickup time passed with no pickup recorded (**Mark picked up**), and those whose return time passed and were never closed (**Close**). Both are the same lists and buttons as Bookings > Now.
- Bookings marked expired or declined that were paid or have a pickup or return report. Only you can say whether it really ran: open the booking.
- Cars on rent with no signed agreement or no deposit.
- Real work routed or credited to a test account, and open tasks or leads assigned to someone who no longer works here (**Unassign** sends it back to its queue).
- Real owner leads whose follow-up stopped before they replied, or never started (**Restart follow-up**), and other leads still new after 2 days.
- Licence reviews waiting more than 24 hours.
- Tasks open twice for the same thing, and open tasks whose subject is already settled, such as "Offer expiring soon" for a car that is already out.
- Published cars missing seats, plate, real photos, a rate card or owner terms, and owners with cars and no terms.
- Payments with no booking, and card processor charges that match no payment.
- Deposits still held 7 days after the car came back.
- Offers that expired more than 48 hours ago still in a queue.
- Real people who asked for a sample car and were not offered a real one yet.
- Email or AI usage on course to go over its included allowance.

## Fixed without asking

Every hour, with the task clean-up, the database fixes what needs no judgment:

- A test account on real work is taken off it, and the work goes back to its queue.
- A duplicate task is closed; the copy being worked, or else the oldest, stays.
- A task whose subject is settled is closed, with the reason in its note.

## Test accounts

The site''s nightly checks sign in with test accounts (addresses starting with verify-, and Resend''s test inboxes). They can still sign in, but no real request, lead, task, commission or notice ever goes to one: the database takes them off at once. **People** > **Portals and view as** marks them "Test account"; staff pickers and sales reports leave them out.',
  '<p class="gd-p">Every night the database checks its own records for the mistakes people used to spot by hand, fixes the clear-cut ones itself and lists the rest for you on one card.</p><section class="gd-task" id="data-health-the-data-health-card" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The Data health card</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Today</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">To do</b>, the Data health card below the usage cards.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The card says when it last checked. Press <b class="gd-ui">Check now</b> to run it again.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Each line is one kind of problem with its count, for example &quot;2 Confirmed bookings whose pickup time passed with no pickup recorded&quot;. All clear shows &quot;All 17 checks clear.&quot;</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press a line to open its records. Each record links to its page.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Where the fix is safe, the record has its button: <b class="gd-ui">Mark picked up</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Close</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Unassign</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Restart follow-up</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Close</b> for a task. The record leaves the card at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The last line says what was fixed without asking this week.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>One in-app notice a day tells Admins when the night&#39;s check found something. It is never emailed or texted.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="data-health-what-it-checks" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">What it checks</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Confirmed bookings whose pickup time passed with no pickup recorded (<b class="gd-ui">Mark picked up</b>), and those whose return time passed and were never closed (<b class="gd-ui">Close</b>). Both are the same lists and buttons as Bookings &gt; Now.</li><li>Bookings marked expired or declined that were paid or have a pickup or return report. Only you can say whether it really ran: open the booking.</li><li>Cars on rent with no signed agreement or no deposit.</li><li>Real work routed or credited to a test account, and open tasks or leads assigned to someone who no longer works here (<b class="gd-ui">Unassign</b> sends it back to its queue).</li><li>Real owner leads whose follow-up stopped before they replied, or never started (<b class="gd-ui">Restart follow-up</b>), and other leads still new after 2 days.</li><li>Licence reviews waiting more than 24 hours.</li><li>Tasks open twice for the same thing, and open tasks whose subject is already settled, such as &quot;Offer expiring soon&quot; for a car that is already out.</li><li>Published cars missing seats, plate, real photos, a rate card or owner terms, and owners with cars and no terms.</li><li>Payments with no booking, and card processor charges that match no payment.</li><li>Deposits still held 7 days after the car came back.</li><li>Offers that expired more than 48 hours ago still in a queue.</li><li>Real people who asked for a sample car and were not offered a real one yet.</li><li>Email or AI usage on course to go over its included allowance.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="data-health-fixed-without-asking" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Fixed without asking</h2><p class="gd-p">Every hour, with the task clean-up, the database fixes what needs no judgment:</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>A test account on real work is taken off it, and the work goes back to its queue.</li><li>A duplicate task is closed; the copy being worked, or else the oldest, stays.</li><li>A task whose subject is settled is closed, with the reason in its note.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="data-health-test-accounts" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Test accounts</h2><p class="gd-p">The site&#39;s nightly checks sign in with test accounts (addresses starting with verify-, and Resend&#39;s test inboxes). They can still sign in, but no real request, lead, task, commission or notice ever goes to one: the database takes them off at once. <b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Portals and view as</b> marks them &quot;Test account&quot;; staff pickers and sales reports leave them out.</p></section>');
